---
import SiteLayout from "@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy — Najd Research"
  description="Privacy commitments for Najd Research products."
>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="page-shell header-inner">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Najd Research home"
        ><img
          class="wordmark-logo"
          src="/logo.webp"
          alt=""
          width="96"
          height="49"
        /><span>Najd Research</span></a
      ><nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="/code">Najd Code <span>01</span></a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main id="main-content" class="document-shell page-shell">
    <header class="document-hero">
      <p class="kicker">POLICY / PRIVACY</p><h1>
        Private work stays private.
      </h1><p class="document-lede">
        Najd products are designed to keep source code, prompts, model outputs,
        paths, filenames, and credentials out of Najd telemetry.
      </p>
    </header>
    <article class="policy-copy">
      <h2>Solo products</h2><p>
        Local inference remains on the device. Cloud providers receive content
        only when a user explicitly enables and selects that provider. Provider
        credentials are stored in the operating system credential store.
      </p>
      <h2>Health telemetry</h2><p>
        Public preview builds send health-only events by default. Najd Code's
        fixed event schema contains the event name, product and version,
        operating system, processor architecture, timestamp, and a random
        installation identifier that rotates every 30 days. Users can disable
        this at any time with the <code>Najd › Health Telemetry: Enabled</code>
        application setting.
      </p><p>
        Health events must not contain prompts, code, model output, repository
        identity, filenames, paths, credentials, or stable hardware identifiers.
        Network addresses are stripped at ingestion and raw events are retained
        for no more than 30 days.
      </p>
      <h2>Enterprise products</h2><p>
        The enterprise control plane stores identity, policy, approvals,
        entitlements, node and repository metadata, and redacted audit events.
        Prompts, code, outputs, artifacts, and provider credentials remain on
        execution nodes.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2><p>
        Privacy questions may be sent to <a
          href="mailto:privacy@najdresearch.com">privacy@najdresearch.com</a
        >.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <footer>
    <div class="page-shell document-footer">
      <p>Najd Research · Riyadh, Saudi Arabia</p><div>
        <a href="/code">Najd Code</a><a href="/security">Security</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</SiteLayout>
